{
 "version": 1,
 "description": "Data-plane scenarios: a Router over a Store with mock providers. Every implementation (memory, PostgreSQL, any other) must reproduce each step. Atoms are decimal strings. A step's expect is a partial match; \"$name\" is an id captured earlier; \">0\" means a positive decimal string. Time-based steps use small durations: virtual clocks advance instantly, SQL stores really sleep.",
